# RX cloud four-stage brightness remap

**Reverted at user request.** The four added BP variables, eight UpdateSky nodes, four material scalar inputs and the full four-stage shader block (including night/transition refinements) were removed. The pre-existing curve-atlas controls, latest Edit05 bake, cloud layout and other sky settings remain. The one-time addition script was removed. The notes below are historical, not the current feature set.

## Scope

- Existing refined shading and the latest Edit04 4K bake were committed and pushed to `main` as `0ba58812d` before this change.
- Added native material scalar parameters and instance-editable float variables to `/Game/RXSkySystem/Cubeless/BP_RXSkySystem_Cubeless`.
- Select `RXSkySystem` in `L_RXSkySystem_Cubeless`, then open the **Cloud Shade Remap** category in Details.
- Variable names, display names and category are English; tooltips are Korean.

| BP parameter | Default | Role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Cloud Remap Deep Shadow | 0 | Deepest shadow output |
| Cloud Remap Shadow | 0.333333 | Shadow output |
| Cloud Remap Midtone | 0.666667 | Midtone output |
| Cloud Remap Highlight | 1 | Highlight output |

The four values interpolate continuously across normalized brightness positions 0, 1/3, 2/3 and 1. They do not posterize the clouds. Lower values blend the corresponding range toward the local sky colour instead of black; higher values brighten it. The slider covers 0–2, with a minimum of 0.

Defaults produce zero correction to the existing shading. The existing curve atlas, sky influence and edge integration remain active. The new remap is evaluated after the atlas and before edge integration. Negative correction blends premultiplied RGB toward `skyBackdrop * coverage`; positive correction adds brightness while retaining hue. Alpha coverage is unchanged. It requires no additional texture sample and no rebake.

## Native implementation and validation

- `M_Cubeless_Clouds_Fog`: four scalar inputs to the existing Custom expression, using piecewise-linear brightness correction.
- `UpdateSky`: four native `MaterialInstanceDynamic.SetScalarParameterValue` calls appended to the existing execution chain, fed by `TODCloudMID` and the instance variables.
- Material and Blueprint compile successfully with zero errors; Blueprint has zero warnings.
- All four variables report `instance_editable=true`. Individually changed each instance value, ran `UpdateSky`, and verified the dynamic material received the expected value. Restored defaults and saved the preview level.
- Fixed camera/motion captures verify a visible response when shadow and midtone values are reduced. The initial before capture has a different viewport resolution, so it is not a pixel-identical before/after test. Default preservation is established by the zero-offset shader construction.
- Recursive asset registry audit found 19 dependencies and no MCP-only reference. Saved functionality uses native Engine nodes; no project C++ changes.
- Full verification passed all 42 checks. The material, Blueprint, level and authoring-script candidate hashes remained unchanged through final validation.
- Evidence: `MCPGameProject/Saved/RXFourStage_20260917/` contains compile results, instance checks, variable metadata, captures, candidate hashes and full verification log.

Authoring script: `scripts/add_rxsky_four_stage_remap_ue.py`. It is a one-time editor authoring script, not a runtime dependency; it refuses to add the block twice.

## Sky-colour correction

The initial brightness-only interpretation was corrected following user review. Low outputs now approach the local sky instead of producing dark holes. The user's current instance values (0, 0.1952, 0.0192, 0.0976) were preserved, verified against the dynamic material, and saved. Fixed-camera captures in `Saved/RXFourStage_20260917/SkyBlend/` show the new colour blending. Korean tooltips describe the revised behaviour. Material and Blueprint compile without errors.

## Night correction

The subsequent user settings (Deep Shadow 1.76, Shadow 1.1248, Midtone 0.3456, Highlight 0.4096) revealed that positive correction adds a daytime white reference even at night. Both four-stage corrections now use `smoothstep(-6, 10, lightEl)`: full effect at solar elevation +10 degrees, smoothly reduced through dusk, zero at -6 degrees and below. Existing night/moon shading is retained. User values are unchanged; the preview time was restored to 14.272 after checking 18:00 and 22:00. Captures in `Saved/RXFourStage_20260917/Night/` verify sunset and night without the excessive pale glow. This changes shading only and needs no rebake.

## Transition refinement (current behaviour)

Audited the four `UpdateSky` setter calls: all have connected execution, `TODCloudMID` targets and their corresponding BP variable inputs. No graph rewiring was needed.

The four-stage classification now uses normalized baked solar transport (`rawSolarTransport / 0.55`) before time-of-day colour grading, rather than the final palette luminance described in the initial implementation above. The output controls retain their identity defaults. Adjacent control offsets use cubic smoothstep interpolation; positive and negative corrections ease through neutral. Sky mixing has a dark-range denominator floor, and positive correction is relative to the current cloud/sky RGB instead of the daytime white floor. This removes the palette feedback and reduces abrupt changes at control boundaries. The night fade remains active, alpha is unchanged, and no texture sample is added.

Rendered checks at 16, 17, 18, 19 and 22 hours are stored under `Saved/RXFourStage_20260917/Transitions/`. These are sampled-time checks, not an exhaustive animation test. User values were retained and time 14.272 restored. No rebake is required.
